Z||000000||KnightRyder31||11-24-2000||11:26 AM||||My Fiero is having difficulties when I try to start it in cold weather. It turns over rather slowly, starts...then dies very fast.<BR>After I start it the 2nd time, I give it some gas, then it barley starts, and runs very crappy until the car has been running for a while.<BR>Please help!||||reg||1
Z||000001||strdream||11-24-2000||12:34 PM||||It shouldn't turn over slowly ever. Sounds like a weak battery, bad starter or cables.<BR>  As for the starting and running bad, are you giving it any gas?  If you are, that will flood it.  Check coolant temp sensor, idle air control. map and tps||||reg||1
Z||000002||KnightRyder31||11-24-2000||05:51 PM||||I have to give it some gas or it doesn't stay running. Then, after it starts...while I'm driving...it has poor response when you give it gas. After it warms up however, everything is normal.||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnnyK||11-24-2000||06:02 PM||||No code by chance saying your running rich?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||11-24-2000||06:29 PM||||Sounds like your cold start system needs help but first we need to know what kind of engine you have||||reg||1
Z||000005||KnightRyder31||11-24-2000||09:11 PM||||1984 2.5L 4cyl Iron Duke TBI injected.||||reg||1
Z||000006||strdream||11-25-2000||02:59 PM||||Giving it gas after it starts is one thing but you shouldn't touch the gas peddle to start it.  I would first look at the coolant temp sensor.  If it is giving the ECM the wrong temp info the fuel mixture will not be right until it worms up, goes into closed loop and the oxygine sensor can tell it how to adjust fuel mixture.  I have also seen condensation in the vac line to the MAP sensor. In freezing wheather the MAP didn't work until the engine heat got to it and melted the ice.  <p>[This message has been edited by strdream (edited 11-25-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||frey||11-27-2000||03:09 AM||||I'm getting the same problem.. doesn't start well when it's cold, and when it is running, either dies, or doesn't take gas as well as it's supposed to..<P>I also get a weird sort of buzzing (sounds like something is spinning too long) noise from the starter for a second or two after I let go of the key<BR>||||reg||1
